                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So, this game looks like a nice little indie game. The title about lucid dreaming (when you know that you are dreaming and can take control of it) sounds interesting. \nBut this game will probably put you back to reality when you encounter the first puzzle.\nI was stuck there because i couldn't figure out the number combination. I had to watch some lets plays to get further. \nI also didn't like the game mechanics: You have to find and take sleep pills to keep a clear vision. Otherwise you can't see anything after a while and die. \nThere's is also a too complex inventory handling in my opinion. To pick up and use a key needs to much steps with pressing buttons and mouse clicks.\nThe game intro seems not to be skippable. So it must be replayed after every quit and restart. It's maybe good to better understand the story when you missed it the first time. But it still gets annoying to do so.\n\nSo this were the main reasons i give a thumb down. But i hope the developers can deal with negative critcs and use them in a constructive way.",
